# Contributing to {{ title }}

## The gate

```console
$ pnpm install                  # once
$ pnpm lint                     # eslint + types + tests
$ cd src-tauri && cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test
```

The same commands CI runs, so a green terminal means a green pull request.
`pnpm dev` runs the interface in a browser, which is faster for pure UI work -
but anything calling into Rust needs the real window, `pnpm tauri dev`.

